; sqrtfull-fp128.cfta - the WHOLE square root on the chip, fp128
;
; python/cft_golden/divfull.py's sqrt_full_program(fp128) as a file:
; the operand raw in r0, the class read off the encoding, the specials
; answered by SELECT in softfloat.sqrt's order (NaN, +-0 as itself, any
; other negative invalid, +inf as itself), a subnormal scaled by an even
; power of two, an odd exponent doubled into [2, 4), the core (seed,
; 4 Newton steps, the half-ulp finish, two restore passes, the exact
; residual and d2), then round_pack in integer instructions. Two
; deposits a lane: the correctly rounded root and its five IEEE flags.
;
; BANK_EXT: the run supplies 49 constants - divfull.bank_sqrt(fp128,
; rnd) - the last five the rounding mode as 0/1 words (RNE, RTZ, RDN,
; RUP, RMM). libcft copies deposit 0 and ORs deposit 1.
;
; The check is byte equality with the image the model generates, and
; the run arm holds the deposits to softfloat.sqrt, specials included.
;
;   r0  a, raw
;   deposits: root, flags

.format   fp128
.deposits 2
.bank     external
.const    k0
.const    k1
.const    k2
.const    k3
.const    k4
.const    k5
.const    k6
.const    k7
.const    k8
